# Anchored with a leading slash so it means the build directory and nothing else.
# Unanchored, `target` matches *any* directory of that name at any depth -- including
# `src/target/`, this crate's bloom-filter module, which it silently excluded.
/target

# Scan output. Named rather than globbed: the old repo used `*.txt*` here, which also
# ignored `assets/wordlist.txt` -- a file `bip39.rs` pulls in with `include_str!` and
# cannot build without. It survived there only because it had been committed before the
# rule existed, so a fresh clone of this repo would have failed to compile.
matches.txt
matches.jsonl
*.state

# Bloom filters. Large, built separately, never committed.
*.bf
*.blf
